SebType's English dictionaries (android/app/src/main/res/raw/main_en.dict and data/en-dict/en_US.dict, built
by data/en-dict/build.sh) take its word frequencies from wordfreq by Robyn Speer (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq), whose
data is under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); the dictionaries' frequencies are shared under the
same licence. en_US.dict's words come from AOSP LatinIME's en_US word list
(dictionaries/en_US_wordlist.combined.gz, Copyright The Android Open Source Project, Apache-2.0). wordfreq contains data from Google Books Ngrams (http://books.google.com/ngrams), the
Leeds Internet Corpus, Wikipedia, ParaCrawl, OPUS OpenSubtitles 2018 (originally from the OpenSubtitles
project, http://www.opensubtitles.org/), Twitter, and the SUBTLEX word lists by Marc Brysbaert et al.
(http://crr.ugent.be/programs-data/subtitle-frequencies), which are freely available data.

